senses.gloss:
प्र-णेजन, अस्, ई, अम्, washing away, wiping
away; (अम्), n. washing away, wiping away, bathing;
water for washing.

प्र-णिपतन, अम्, n. falling down before, throw-
ing one's self down at any one's feet, prostration;
bowing or doing homage to, saluting.

प्रणिशम् प्र-णि-शम्, cl. 4. P. -शाम्यति,
-शमितुम्, to become calm, be pacified or appeased;
to hear.

प्र-णयन, अम्, n. bringing forwards, conduct-
ing; conveying, bringing, fetching [cf. अग्नि-षोम-
प्˚]; carrying out, executing, performing, practising;
bringing forward, adducing; composing, writing;
that in which anything is brought [cf. प्रणीता-प्˚];
dispensing, distributing; decreeing, awarding, sen-
tencing; (with दण्डस्य or दण्ड-प्˚) carrying
the rod, inflicting punishment.

प्राणक, अस्, m. a living being, an animal or
sentient being; a species of plant (= जीवक); myrrh;
cloth, clothes (?).
